Package: par2circadian
Title: AR(2) Eigenvalue Persistence Analysis of Circadian Time Series
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Michael", "Whiteside", email = "mickwh@msn.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-0643-5791"))
Description: Estimates temporal persistence in gene expression time series by
    fitting a second-order autoregressive model per gene and reporting the
    eigenvalue modulus of its characteristic equation. Conventional circadian
    methods answer whether a gene cycles; the eigenvalue modulus instead
    measures how strongly recent expression constrains future expression, which
    separates clock genes from their targets and from background in intact
    tissue. Provides single-series and matrix-wide fitting, root-type
    classification, half-life and intrinsic-period conversions,
    residual-bootstrap confidence intervals for short series, and hierarchy
    summaries. Numerically equivalent to the reference Python implementation
    'par2-circadian'. The method is described in Whiteside (2026)
    <doi:10.21203/rs.3.rs-9283100/v1>.
